Day 30 – DAX Measures for HR Analytics Dashboard

Project Overview

On Day 30 of my Unguided Data Analytics Projects, I focused on building DAX measures in Power Pivot to support an HR analytics dashboard.

Instead of jumping straight into visuals, I worked on defining the core business metrics that would drive the insights behind the dashboard.

This step is important because strong dashboards start with well-defined measures and calculations.

⸻

Dataset

The dataset contains HR employee information including:
	•	Employee ID
	•	Age
	•	Gender
	•	Marital Status
	•	Branch
	•	Hire Date
	•	Leave Date
	•	Department
	•	Salary
	•	Total Compensation

The dataset is used to analyze workforce structure, attrition, and compensation metrics.
Total Employees = COUNTROWS(Employees)
Active Employees =
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Employees),
    Employees[Attrition] = "No"
)
Attrition =
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Employees),
    Employees[Attrition] = "Yes"
)